WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.100
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.621
Last time we met the people.

5
00:00:10.621 --> 00:00:13.553
Today, the rest of the people folder: types, factions,

6
00:00:13.553 --> 00:00:16.703
and the notes Voyage uses when it makes people up for you.

7
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.683
Open Characters, then NPCs, then NPC Settings.

8
00:00:21.683 --> 00:00:29.083
Up top, two numbers: the health every N P C starts from, and how much more they get each level.

9
00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:33.767
Next, back under NPC Settings, open NPC Types.

10
00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:40.440
A type is a kind of creature or person that shares a damage profile, so you only set it once.

11
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.598
We've got Road Bandits and Gloamwood Things.

12
00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:47.502
The description says what they are and how they act.

13
00:00:47.502 --> 00:00:49.303
Bandits can be talked down.

14
00:00:49.303 --> 00:00:50.837
Gloamwood Things can't.

15
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.581
Then what hurts them.

16
00:00:52.581 --> 00:00:58.008
Gloamwood Things are weak to fire and light, shrug off piercing, and poison does nothing.

17
00:00:58.008 --> 00:01:02.155
Every N P C of that type gets this, plus anything on their own card.

18
00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:05.954
Factions live under NPC Settings too.

19
00:01:05.954 --> 00:01:10.405
A faction is a group with its own aims, and people can belong to one.

20
00:01:10.405 --> 00:01:13.566
Both shows are in here, ours and the Gilt Circus,

21
00:01:13.566 --> 00:01:17.889
and I've put myself and Marla in the show and Lucius in the circus.

22
00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:23.221
Basic info is the public face, what the towns think of them.

23
00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.784
Faction type. Major shows as World in the journal,

24
00:01:26.784 --> 00:01:30.526
and Voyage hands it to the AI when it makes up a new region.

25
00:01:30.526 --> 00:01:31.835
Minor shows as Local.

26
00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:38.437
Hidden info is what's really going on, and the best ones have something happening right now.

27
00:01:38.437 --> 00:01:43.039
The Gilt Circus is going broke, and it's got someone inside our show.

28
00:01:44.433 --> 00:01:46.282
Two tips from Voyage's docs.

29
00:01:46.282 --> 00:01:51.169
Give each faction a World Lore entry with the same name and the same text,

30
00:01:51.169 --> 00:01:53.481
so the narrator finds it both ways.

31
00:01:53.481 --> 00:01:58.896
And a faction that starts hidden is found the moment the story says its full name,

32
00:01:58.896 --> 00:02:01.802
so don't call your secret society The Watch.

33
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.200
Under NPC Settings, then Advanced, then NPC Archetypes.

34
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.527
These are personality templates.

35
00:02:09.527 --> 00:02:15.708
Voyage ships twenty-two of them, so it's a long list, and the search box finds yours.

36
00:02:15.708 --> 00:02:17.817
I added one called Show Folk.

37
00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:21.370
Drives, traits, morality and relationships.

38
00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:26.278
When Voyage fleshes out a person it made up, it picks one at random,

39
00:02:26.278 --> 00:02:29.598
and only for the tougher tiers, strong and up.

40
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.486
And next door, NPC Author Seeds.

41
00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:38.070
Each one is a writing style for the people Voyage makes up.

42
00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:43.586
Voyage ships nineteen, mostly named after writers like Joe Abercrombie,

43
00:02:43.586 --> 00:02:47.005
and it's another long list, so search again.

44
00:02:47.005 --> 00:02:48.870
Mine's called Road Show.

45
00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:54.875
Five short lines: what you show them through, what you focus on, what they do.

46
00:02:54.875 --> 00:02:58.640
Same deal, one picked at random, strong tiers and up.

47
00:03:00.033 --> 00:03:02.244
That's the people folder done.

48
00:03:02.244 --> 00:03:07.401
Our types, factions, archetype and seed are linked in the description.

49
00:03:07.401 --> 00:03:13.222
Next time, the player: premade characters, random names and character creation.

50
00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:17.615
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

